{"availability":"available","full":"tylerLiCodes/Flyguard","name":"Flyguard","description":"Autonomous drone horn-fly laser defense for cattle farms","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":84,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-01T18:03:30Z","updated":"2026-06-01T19:49:03Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tylerlicodes.github.io/flyguard-web/","topics":[],"demo":"https://tylerlicodes.github.io/flyguard-web/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T05:02:14.254Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T05:02:14.254Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T05:02:14.254Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:42.429Z","stars":84,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:14:40.642Z","stars":84,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-19T05:02:14.254Z","stars":84,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Autonomous drone horn-fly laser defense for cattle farms","Horn flies (Haematobia irritans) are among the costliest cattle pests, driving weight loss, reduced milk yield, and disease. Flyguard flies an autonomous patrol over a pasture, analyzes the video feed to detect and track horn flies on cattle, and neutralizes them with a gimbal-aimed laser — while treating cattle and humans as protected entities that are never targeted.","⚠️ A laser that kills a fly is a Class 3B/4 eye hazard."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tylerLiCodes/Flyguard/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"310aa4508e1e8c8187faa95013e98fcf9e3593061b76a529792772f93205302a","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:42.621Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:42.621Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Autonomous drone horn-fly laser defense for cattle farms","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tylerLiCodes/Flyguard/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"310aa4508e1e8c8187faa95013e98fcf9e3593061b76a529792772f93205302a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tylerLiCodes/Flyguard/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:42.621